GOAL : Make a better stocksim (make it both visual and make the code more efficient)
Learn: some database method

1. Import a free finance API (yfinance) and create a function to gte the price, it will try to get the fastest, most recent price based on the ticker symbol, if it cant find the price then it will look at the history to get the price and if both methods dont work then in tehory the ticker is not real therfore it returns it as an error / 0.
2. TickerTracker Class, I need a class to find out everything i need to display when it comes to the ticker. To get the methods you need to enter a ticker, the amount, and the avg price which i will get later with the yfinace function. Errors are returned if an input is incorrect. get_entire_cost method: amount x price. update current price method: takes the new current price and changes the current price into it. profit n loss and percentage: (made to be displayed visually later), takes current market price - price they bought * by the amount they bought and made into a percentage in the other method. repr was used to test it.
3. User Class, The most important class which allows this project to actually function. Allows for a input of a name, and start money (defaults at 10k). Also gave it a inv dictionary attribute to store what the user owns. BUY Method: requires input of ticker, amount bought and the value of each ticker. If the user has less money than required then a value error is raised, otherwise then the user's money is updated. If the ticker is not inside of the dictionary then it creates a ticker object and puts the ticker as the key for it. Otherwise if the ticker is already in the invintory of the user it will get the ticker object(value of tracked inv ticker) and it will calculate the new cost by adding the bought value to the value thats already there and same with the amount. Then it will update the attributes of the object thats linked to the tracked inv ticker. SELL method: requires the same input as the buying method. 3 options. 1: not in inv = raises a value error. 2: Inside of the inv but not enough to be sold = raises a value error, 3. Can be sold = the user's money increases and the amount in the inv of that specific ticker decreases based on it. And if the amount of the ticker reaches 0 the ticker is deleted from the inv.

PYGAME - CREATING THE VISUALS
4. Sidebar, Created a user profile rectangle which will include the user's name, amount of money they current have and how much total profit the user has mamaged to amass overtime. Then there is the 'buy' rectangle where an emoji of a shopping cart is used from the base computer emoji set (part of the fonts) and when the mouse position is hovering over this rectangle the retangle will go from black to a dark grey (40,40,40). Then this exact same process is repeated for the sell and portfolio sidebar rectangles with the minor difference of the emoji and text.
5. Buy game state, when the user clicks on the buy rectangle on the sidebar it changes the gamestate to 'buy'. In this gamestate the title at the top will be 'buy' with a breif explanation of what the user can accomplish in this page. There are 2 rectangles with allow the user to input the company name, then the quantity that they wish to buy. In the company_input_rect the user is able to change the [enter company...] text into whatver they user is typing, this is the same with the [enter quantity] buy_amount_rect. When the user uses backspace while typing it does [:-1] which removes the last letter in the string, and when the user clicks enter it saves the company name into the varibale called buy_input_results while for the amount they buy it is stored in the varibale buyamount_input_results.
6. Created a confirm button. This button will complete the buying method from the classes_function file (User class), this will then update the user's money etc which is explained in step 3. There are also error statements that will be blitted when one opf the inputs from the boxes are incorret this will be in the middle and below both of the boxes (ensures that the inputs are corret before completeing the buy method)
7. When the player clicks enter in the company text box, there will be red and green boxes in which will fluctate based on the ticker's price in the last month (day intervals). In the classes_dunction file, get_stock_history will get the data for the past month however this will require the user to have interent and for there to be no issues so if something goes wrong there is a set of dummy data that can be used.
8. Creating a red and green boxes which have variable heights depedning on the last month prices of the ticker. When the user  clicks return once they've entered a company the graph will blit. When the user clicks return their input will be vhanged into a ticker or validated by the records file, if the ticker is invalid an error message will appear with a dummy set of values. whereas if the user enters a valid company then the ticker will be put into the get_stock_history function which will retunr of list oif values of the compnay in teh past month. There are variables for the start x/y, spacing etc for the visuals once it is blit. A minimum and maximum value are gotten and a ratio is cretaed to essentaite the price difference later. It then enumerates thorugh the index and the prices to get the colour of the box, if its lower then it will be red while if its hgher than the last day it will be green. The bar hieght will be determined by teh base height, ratio and the swing hight(the height added from the lowest to the highest). The x pos will increase once the index number increases and the y pos will be determined by minuising from the bar hieght. This is then blit with the correct values.
